# Build context for the CBB engine sweep image (Dockerfile.cbb).
#
# Rule: the image must contain everything the ENGINE opens at sim time
# (traced by reading scripts/run_engine.py + src/cbb_sim/engine/{inputs,
# adapters}.py -- see docs/ops/aws_launch_chain.md section 1) and nothing
# that could change what it computes or that leaks a secret.

# --- Secrets. Never, under any circumstance, in the image. ----------------
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem

# --- Host-specific / rebuildable ------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
logs/

# --- Gitignored bulk data NOT needed at sim time. The engine's own inputs
# under data/processed/models/engine/ (including the gitignored
# event_round2_s1_F2_2025/ S1 artifact tree) are intentionally NOT excluded
# here -- they must be present on disk when `docker build` runs.
data/raw/
data/hoopr/

# --- Prior results: never bake sweep OUTPUT into the image. Outputs live on
# the mounted /out volume; a baked-in results/ would risk being mistaken for
# a resumed/completed run. (CBB's run_engine.py does not itself resume from
# a partial results dir the way cfb's build_sweep_dist_v10.py does, but the
# principle -- outputs are not inputs -- still holds.)
results/**

# --- Rebuildable large intermediates the engine never reads at sim time ----
data/processed/possessions/
data/processed/possessions_v2/
data/processed/models/**/design.parquet
data/processed/models/**/*_design.parquet

# --- Nothing here is read by the engine -----------------------------------
out.md
*.bat
